   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,121:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: THE DROPOUT SIGNAL
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,143:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: An AI-Powered Early Warning System for Student Retention
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,153:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: HackBricks 2026 — Problem Statement 1
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PART 1: THE PROBLEM
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Why This Matters
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7 million students
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,216:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  drop out of Indian higher education every year (AISHE 2023)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: India
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,226:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,228:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s gross enrollment ratio is 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,231:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 28.4%
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — already low. Dropouts make it worse.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,258:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: NEP 2020
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,260:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  explicitly mandates universities to reduce dropout rates
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,261:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,264:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: NAAC accreditation tracks dropout rates — universities are measured on this
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Hidden Truth
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,268:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Dropout is never sudden. The warning signs appear 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,270:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: months before
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,271:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: :
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,277:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Semester 1 grade: 14.2 → Semester 2 grade: 9.8 (declining trajectory)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,303:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,306:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Tuition fee: UNPAID for 2 months (financial stress)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,308:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,313:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Age at enrollment: 34 (mature student, likely working, higher drop risk)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,315:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,317:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Parent occupation: unskilled labor (first-generation college student)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,319:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,322:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: GDP dropped 2.3% (macroeconomic pressure on family income)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The data exists in every university
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,326:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,328:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s Student Information System (SIS). But 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,332:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: nobody connects the dots
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,344:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Registrars
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,350:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: see grades. Finance sees fees. Counselors see who walks in. Nobody sees the full picture.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,354:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Challenge Beyond Prediction
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,359:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A model that predicts dropout is easy. A model that is 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,362:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: FAIR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,363:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is hard.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,365:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A model that disproportionately flags students from lower-income backgrounds or specific
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,382:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: demographics is a liability, not a tool.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,385:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,388:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,391:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: — HackBricks Problem Statement
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,433:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Historical data encodes historical bias. If low-income students dropped out more in the past, a naive model will flag
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,437:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: them at higher rates — even when their current performance is identical to wealthier peers. The model becomes a 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,440:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: self-fulfilling prophecy of inequality
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,442:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,444:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Our pipeline must:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,448:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,450:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Predict risk early
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,453:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,456:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Explain WHY (not just a number)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,457:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,460:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Prove
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,463:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  it is not biased against any group
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,465:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,467:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Validate
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,469:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  predictions through direct, unbiased student conversations
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,470:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,473:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Connect
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,475:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  at-risk students to the RIGHT resources based on WHY they
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,477:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,478:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: re leaving
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,482:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: THE COLLEGE DATA PIPELINE — HOW DATA ACTUALLY FLOWS
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:53,485:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How Colleges Work Today (The Gap We Fill)
