   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,379:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,382:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  3. ML MODELS — Two Required by Problem Statement       │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,384:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │                                                         │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,387:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  Model A: Logistic Regression (BASELINE)                │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,389:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │     • Interpretable, fast, regularized                  │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,391:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │     • Log: accuracy, precision, recall, F1, AUC-ROC     │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,393:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │     • Logged in MLflow Experiment                        │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,397:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │                                                         │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,399:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  Model B: XGBoost (TREE MODEL)                          │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,402:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │     • Gradient boosted trees, handles non-linearity     │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,404:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │     • Hyperparameter tuning logged                      │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,406:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │     • Logged in MLflow Experiment                        │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,409:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │                                                         │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,413:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  COMPARE → Register BEST model in Model Registry        │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,415:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  (Champion model served for inference)                   │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,417:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,419:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:                            │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,421:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:                            ▼
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,423:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,426:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  4. FAIRNESS AUDIT — 25% of Evaluation Score!           │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,429:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │                                                         │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,431:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  Compute across Gender AND Socioeconomic groups:        │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,433:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │                                                         │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,438:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  • Demographic Parity Ratio                             │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,440:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │    "Does the model flag men and women at similar rates?" │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,444:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │    Formula: P(flagged | Group A) / P(flagged | Group B) │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,447:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │    Target: ratio between 0.8 and 1.25 = FAIR            │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,450:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │                                                         │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,455:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  • Equal Opportunity Ratio                              │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,460:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │    "Among actual dropouts, does the model catch them    │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,464:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │     equally across groups?"                             │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,467:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │    Formula: TPR(Group A) / TPR(Group B)                 │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,469:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │    Target: ratio between 0.8 and 1.25 = FAIR            │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,471:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │                                                         │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,474:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  • Log ALL metrics to fairness_audit Delta table        │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,476:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  • If biased → DOCUMENT IT (do not hide)                │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,478:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     │  • Propose mitigation: threshold tuning, reweighting    │
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,480:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,481:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:                            │
