   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,748:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: our model flagged you.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,750:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,752:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  They say 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,755:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,761:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: I found some
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: resources that might help.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,768:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,771:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,773:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Impact:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,779:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Someone asked. Someone listened. Someone connected them to SPECIFIC help. They
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: stay.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,786:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,788:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Quote:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,790:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,791:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,794:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The college called and asked how I was doing. Then my advisor found me a scholarship I
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,797:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: didn
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,799:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,800:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t know existed. I almost quit — but now I
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,802:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,805:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: m staying.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PART 4: FEATURE ENGINEERING — Our Creativity Edge
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,814:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Original Features in Dataset (37 columns)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Demographics, academic grades (Semester 1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,819:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,826:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 across subjects), financial flags (tuition, debtor, scholarship),
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,829:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: macroeconomic context (GDP, unemployment, inflation).
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,832:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Our Engineered Features (the 20% creativity score)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,835:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Grade Trajectory Slope
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Not just "what is their grade?" but "are they improving or
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: declining?"
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Student A: Sem1 = 14, Sem2 = 14  →  slope = 0.0  (stable)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,848:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Student B: Sem1 = 14, Sem2 = 9   →  slope = -5.0 (declining — HIGH
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,850:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: RISK)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,853:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Student C: Sem1 = 9,  Sem2 = 13  →  slope = +4.0 (improving — LOW RISK)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,854:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Formula: mean(Sem2 grades) - mean(Sem1 grades)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,857:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: WHY: A declining student with a 12 average is MORE at risk than 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,859:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      a stable student with a 10 average. Trajectory > snapshot.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,862:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. Financial Stress Index
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,866:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Combines 4+ signals into one composite score:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,869:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: financial_stress = (
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,873:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     tuition_not_paid × 0.35     # 35% weight — strongest signal
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,875:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     + debtor_flag × 0.25        # 25% weight — existing debt
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,879:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     + (1 - scholarship) × 0.20  # 20% weight — no scholarship = more
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: stress
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,883:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     + inflation_rate × 0.10     # 10% weight — macro pressure
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,885:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:     + (1/GDP_growth) × 0.10     # 10% weight — economic downturn
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,887:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: )
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,889:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: WHY: A student with unpaid tuition in a recession year with no 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,891:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      scholarship is under EXTREME financial pressure. No single 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,893:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      feature captures this — the composite does.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,894:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3. Curricular Engagement Ratio
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,897:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: engagement_ratio = units_approved / units_enrolled
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,900:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Student A: enrolled in 6 courses, approved 6  →  ratio = 1.0
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,901:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (engaged)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,903:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Student B: enrolled in 6 courses, approved 2  →  ratio = 0.33
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,905:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (disengaged)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,910:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: WHY: Low approval rate = student is not keeping up. Strong
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,911:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: predictor 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,915:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      of withdrawal — they're already mentally checked out.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,917:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. Semester-over-Semester Grade Delta
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,919:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For each subject area, compute: Sem2_grade - Sem1_grade
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,921:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Curricular Unit 1: Sem1 = 15, Sem2 = 12  →  delta = -3
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,923:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Curricular Unit 2: Sem1 = 13, Sem2 = 8   →  delta = -5
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,926:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: avg_grade_delta = mean(all deltas) = -4.0
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,930:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: WHY: Consistent decline across ALL subjects is a stronger signal 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      than decline in one subject (which could be a hard course).
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5. Economic Pressure Index
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: economic_pressure = unemployment_rate × inflation_rate / GDP_growth
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,941:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: High unemployment + high inflation + low GDP = MAXIMUM pressure
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,946:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: WHY: A student whose family is under economic stress is more likely
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,949:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,952:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      to drop out to work, even if their grades are acceptable.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,955:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6. Age Risk Indicator
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,958:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: age_risk = 1 if age_at_enrollment > 25 else 0
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,963:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: WHY: Mature students (working adults, parents) have competing 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,968:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      responsibilities. Research shows 25+ age is a consistent 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,970:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:      dropout risk factor.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,973:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PART 5: FAIRNESS AUDIT — The Winning Differentiator
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,975:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Why This Is 25% of the Score
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,978:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Most hackathon teams train a model and show accuracy. 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,979:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We prove ours is fair.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,982:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The problem statement explicitly warns:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,983:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,993:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A model that disproportionately flags students from lower-income backgrounds or specific
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,994:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: demographics is a liability, not a tool.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,997:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:54,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What We Audit
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,000:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Protected Attributes:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,003:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,005:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Gender
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,007:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (Male / Female)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,009:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,011:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Socioeconomic group
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,014:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — derived from: scholarship holder + parent occupation + tuition payment status
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Metrics We Compute:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,021:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A. Demographic Parity Ratio
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,023:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Question: "Does the model flag men and women at similar rates?"
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,027:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            P(flagged as at-risk | Female)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,029:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   DPR  =  ─────────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            P(flagged as at-risk | Male)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,034:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   FAIR if: 0.8 ≤ DPR ≤ 1.25
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,036:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   UNFAIR if: DPR < 0.8 or DPR > 1.25
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,038:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Example:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,043:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   Model flags 22% of females, 25% of males  →  DPR = 0.88  ✅ FAIR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,047:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   Model flags 35% of females, 15% of males  →  DPR = 2.33  ❌ UNFAIR
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,050:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: B. Equal Opportunity Ratio
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,053:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Question: "Among students who ACTUALLY dropped out, does the 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,055:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            model catch them equally across groups?"
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,057:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            TPR(Female)    True Positive Rate for females
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,061:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   EOR  =  ───────────  = ──────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            TPR(Male)      True Positive Rate for males
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,066:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   FAIR if: 0.8 ≤ EOR ≤ 1.25
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,068:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   UNFAIR if: EOR < 0.8 or EOR > 1.25
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,070:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Example:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,072:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   Model catches 85% of female dropouts, 82% of male dropouts
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   →  EOR = 1.04  ✅ FAIR (catches both groups equally)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,077:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: C. Predictive Parity
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Question: "When the model says HIGH risk, is it equally accurate 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,083:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            for all groups?"
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,084:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            Precision(Group A)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,086:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   PPR  =  ──────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            Precision(Group B)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   If model says "HIGH risk" for females but is wrong 40% of the
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,090:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: time,
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,092:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   while being wrong only 10% for males → model is unfairly alarming 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,094:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:   female students. 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,096:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How We Report It
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,097:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: All metrics are saved to a 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,099:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: fairness
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,101:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,102:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: audit
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,104:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Delta table:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,105:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | model
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,108:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: name | attribute | group
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,109:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,110:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: a | group
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,111:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,113:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: b | metric | value | is
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,114:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,115:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: fair |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,117:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,119:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |-----------|-----------|---------|---------|--------|-------|---------|
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,120:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,122:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | xgboost
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,123:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,124:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: v1 | gender | Female | Male | demographic
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,125:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,129:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: parity | 0.88 | YES |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,130:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,132:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | xgboost
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,133:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,135:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: v1 | gender | Female | Male | equal
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,136:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,138:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: opportunity | 1.04 | YES |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,139:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,141:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | xgboost
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,142:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,144:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: v1 |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,146:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: socioeconomic | low
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,147:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: income | high
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,150:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,151:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: income | demographic
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,153:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,154:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: parity | 1.42 | NO |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If We Find Bias (We Probably Will)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: We don
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,159:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,161:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t hide it.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The PDF says 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,164:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,167:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: document any disparity found.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,167:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If the model over-flags low-income students:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,171:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,173:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Document it
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,175:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,176:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Model flags 38% of low-income vs 18% of high-income (DPR = 2.11)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,180:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,184:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Explain why
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Historical data shows low-income students dropped out more; model learned this
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: bias
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Propose mitigation:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Threshold adjustment: use different risk thresholds per group
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Sample reweighting: upweight underrepresented groups in training
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,211:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Feature removal: drop direct socioeconomic features, keep only academic signals
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,216:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Show the trade-off
