   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,530:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: LAYER 2: AI VOICE VERIFICATION — THE INNOVATION THAT
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,532:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHANGES EVERYTHING
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,533:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Problem With Layer 1 Alone
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,539:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Every ML model has false positives. A student might show declining grades because:
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,542:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,544:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: They switched majors (not dropout risk — just a transition)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,547:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,549:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: They had a medical emergency (temporary, will recover)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,552:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,554:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The semester was genuinely harder (course difficulty, not student failure)
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,558:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If a counselor calls 200 students based on ML alone, 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,560:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 30-40% may be false alarms
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,569:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . After a few wrong calls,
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,571:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: counselors lose trust in the system. Game over.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,573:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Layer 2: AI-Powered Student Conversation
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:55,577:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: After Layer 1 flags a student as HIGH risk (score > 0.7), our AI voice agent calls them.
