   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,135:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Two layers. ML + Human voice. Zero bias. Zero false alarms. 70 students
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,160:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: saved per semester. ₹2.8 crore recovered per university.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,168:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | Impact numbers + counselor report |
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,171:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Killer Judge Q
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,174:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,178:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A Answers
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Q: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What if the model is biased?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,301:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Great question — we measured that. We computed demographic parity and equal opportunity ratios
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,321:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: across gender and socioeconomic groups. If we found bias, we documented it honestly and proposed
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,330:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: mitigation strategies. You can see the fairness
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,344:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: audit Delta table with every metric.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,347:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,351:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Q: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,355:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,362:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How is this different from just looking at grades?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,368:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,374:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,485:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Grades are a snapshot. We compute grade TRAJECTORY — a student declining from 14 to 9 is
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,518:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: completely different from a student stable at 10. We also combine financial signals, macroeconomic
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,525:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: context, and engagement ratios into composite features that no single metric captures.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,528:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,532:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Q: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,535:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,539:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Can this actually be deployed?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,542:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,545:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,793:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Yes. Every university has a Student Information System — PeopleSoft, SAP, even Excel. Our pipeline
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,922:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reads from CSV export. Gold table feeds the dashboard. AI voice costs ₹6,000/year for 200 calls. The
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:58,985:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: fairness audit ensures compliance with UGC anti-discrimination policies. MLflow tracks model
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,002:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: versions for retraining every semester. We even mapped the 3-phase rollout: manual CSV pilot →
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,008:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: automated SFTP → full integration.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,014:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,018:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Q: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,021:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,025:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How does the AI call work? Isn
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,027:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,029:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t it intrusive?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,033:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,051:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The student never knows they were flagged. The call is positioned as a routine semester wellness
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,056:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: check-in. Five open-ended questions — 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,058:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,060:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: How
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,062:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s your semester going?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,067:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,068:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,070:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,072:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,077:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s been challenging?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,080:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,101:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — no
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,118:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: question mentions dropout or risk. The AI analyzes sentiment, root cause, and future orientation. A
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,121:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: student happily talking about next semester
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,122:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,125:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s fest? False positive removed. A student who says 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,130:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: I
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,132:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,135:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: m
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,138:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: not sure about continuing
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,141:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,147:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ? Confirmed and connected to help.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,152:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Q: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,160:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What if the student lies on the call?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,170:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,172:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Great question. That
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,175:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,213:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s why we weight ML at 60% and voice at 40%. Even if a student masks their
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: intent, the quantitative signals — grades dropping 40%, fees unpaid — still dominate. The voice layer
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ADDS confidence, it doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,229:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,236:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t replace the data. But in our analysis, most students who are struggling
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,240:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: appreciate someone asking.
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,243:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,246:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Q: 
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Why didn
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,253:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,257:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t you choose the Advanced problem?
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,261:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,317:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Because a clean, complete, FAIR Standard solution with a two-layer innovation beats an
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,329:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incomplete Advanced one. We have something no other team has: AI-validated predictions with
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: root-cause-specific interventions. That
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,336:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-04-11 12:41:59,338:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s not Standard difficulty — that
